invariant: INV-16
file: p256_wide_point.c
catches: p256_equiv_test
reason: the Jacobian doubling leaves out the step that makes m three
  times (X1 - zz) (X1 + zz), so m is twice that, and X3 and Y3 come out
  for another point. No fault follows: every coordinate is still a field
  element. bin/p256_equiv_test holds the doubling to the complete
  addition of a point with itself on multiples of G, and every key
  exchange doubles 253 times.

--- old
    p256_wide_fe_add(&t, &m, &m);
    p256_wide_fe_add(&m, &t, &m);
--- new
    p256_wide_fe_add(&m, &m, &m);
